I suppose that what is meant is the right words, not just the number.  The 
autogenerated ones would not be intelligible Lojban, even if they were 
well-formed.  The claim is basically, that we aren't "finished" because we 
haven't talked enough about enough things, certainly that there are things 
talked about in other languages which have never been mentioned in Lojban and 
yet are in the realm o fLojbanists' experiences (this to keep Piranha finished 
even though no one has talked about nuclear physics -- or plain physics -- in 
it).  That we could talk about these, were we inclined to, without adding 
anything to the language but new words formed to established formats doesn't 
count.  Of course, with a little thought, we could probably come up with some 
areas of experience never talked about in English  -- but it would be a lot 
harder.




